{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310735,"nonce":"gIQeTMwthWxtYtjFK6oDoE+uUuA=","title":"The runtime's user-space stdout buffer is never flushed at process exit, so a trailing Sys.print with no newline emits zero bytes","message":"VERIFIED, 4 lines, exit 0:\n\n    class Main { static function main() { Sys.print(\"no-newline-payload\"); } }\n\ncaptures **0 bytes**. `Sys.println` of the same string captures it fine.\n\n`runtime/src/haxe_string.rs:54` keeps a user-space stdout buffer with a 50 ms\nflush interval; `haxe_string_print` (:756) sets `force` only when the slice\ncontains `\\n`, and `haxe_string_println` (:767) forces unconditionally. Nothing\nflushes at process exit, so any trailing unforced write is lost.\n\nThis is silent output loss, and being timing-dependent it is machine-dependent —\nthe \"exit 0, no output\" signature. It is a PLAUSIBLE but UNPROVEN mechanism for\nthe three tests that score NO_OUTPUT only on the CI runner\n([[bugs_mac_and_linux_conformance_are_identical]]); the conformance marker itself\ngoes through `println`, so it is forced, and the trio was NOT explained by this.\nDo not close that anomaly on this basis without reproducing it.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_trailing_sys_print_is_discarded_at_exit` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}